{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"DM radar","id":"313689699627696139","is_bot":0,"username":"bfdm"},"author_id":"313689699627696139","channel_id":"746813707803295744","content":"Hart Island NAME ORIGIN Believed to refer to its population of deer (hart is an archaic word for deer). HISTORY During the Civil War, the island was used by the Federal Government to house troops and was a prison for Confederate soldiers. Potters' Field was established around 1865 when some soldiers, victims of an epidemic, were interred there. The city acquired the island in 1869; since then, there have been over half a million burials. Around 1872, the island was used for the detention of \"vicious boys,\" and over the years also housed minor criminals, vagrants and drug addicts.","created_at":"2020-08-24T03:11:51.903000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"747292063288000532","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
